{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters","id":1543052,"title":"[Curseborne] Supplement Idea \u2013 Mortal Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-03T03:52:17-07:00","id":1543052,"title":"[Curseborne] Supplement Idea \u2013 Mortal Hunters","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Now reading The World chapter of <b>CB</b> corebook, I easily see we need playable mortal hunters book down the line. ( Probably similar to Tier 1 of Hunter the Vigil. ) Even <b>CB</b> corebook text directly points they are rather often phenomena.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>\u2019Curseborne KS preview \u2013 The World\u2019</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">People accept phantasms are real, or at least accept that other people accept them as real, even if they don\u2019t believe they are. Even the most skeptical person has a story about a spooky place they went to that gave them chills. Everyone has a friend who lived in a haunted house once, or who met a ghost. <b>Ghost hunting shows are some of the most popular media on television, past reality TV.</b> They\u2019re common enough that most people can name a handful of haunted sites in their cities. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Few phantasms want to be the subject of <b>some mortal\u2019s curiosity, summoning, interrogation, and attempts at exorcism, </b>so their reactions tend toward the hostile. Depending on the phantasm, they\u2019re aware that there\u2019s no other fate for them beyond this existence (or if there is, no phantasms out there claim to have visited and returned), so they make the best of a squalid situation. That means either accepting a person into their home or driving enquiring humans away. People who choose to live in a phantasm\u2019s abode and show them respect often find living alongside them easy, and often barely even recognize the phantasm is there<b>. Disruptive people</b> are subjected to a combination of nightmares, telekinesis, mental suggestion, or possession to scare them away. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(\u2026)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Phantasms appear in everything </b>from novels, video games, and movies (more being based on fragments of true stories than not) to low budget docuseries popular on streaming sites and shorts on social media. Everyone\u2019s seen that one Greatest Enigmas episode where those <b>na\u00efve film students went stumbling around a caved in mine</b> and ended up losing their lives one by one, some through their own idiocy, others because the phantasms of the dead miners just wanted to be left in peace. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T04:36:34-07:00","id":1543054,"title":"","content":"This makes sense. It fits logically and thematically for their to be hunters. You'll need three basic types. Non supernatural hunters of different levels of training who have chosen or been drafted to fight the monsters. Buffy-type supernaturals empowered to protect humans. And finally Curseborns who stand up to exploitive curseborns and say enough! The second two categories would be both protecting normals and non threatening Curseborns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T07:40:17-07:00","id":1543057,"title":"","content":"Interesting would be Lineages Path changes - Buffy-type ( Tier 2? ) would need specific 'monster' Linage ( like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1537549-fan-mortal-hunters-linage\"><b>one I proposed earlier</b></a> ). But Mortal ( Tier 1 ) hunters would need to have other Path variant here - as the are no 'monster' Linage - and they already have Role Path, as all characters in CB mechanics. Maybe 'hunting type' here? Like how PC is hunting things in darkness? Stalker, Charmer, Analyst? But would this also double Role Path in the end? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T09:06:17-07:00","id":1543061,"title":"","content":"I started a thing about mortal hunter-adjacent lineage a ways back, and working on one that will be compatable with the manuscript. If anyone wants to help throw suggestions for fan made product to cover the niche until then... that'd be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T10:57:29-07:00","id":1543066,"title":"","content":"Doesn\u2019t playable mortal hunters kinda go against the theme of Curseborne? Like the unifitying theme as to why characters of different families and lineages working together is they are all Accursed. That\u2019s where their magic comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T11:56:52-07:00","id":1543067,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think that mortal hunters would undermine the themes of Curseborne. You have. You have a number of supernatural creatures out there, some of which surely engage in some pretty bad misbehavior - certainly some humans are going to fight back.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that it\u2019s necessarily needed at this point though. I think that The Hunters Hunter was a good supplement for V:tM back in the day and I think something like that for Curseborne would be cool. I don\u2019t think that supernatural hunters should be their creature type.<br /> <br /> Curseborne can also hunt each other for any number or noble or ignoble reasons. An angelic combat Outcast who protects humans from evil Curseborne would fit that archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T07:03:30-07:00","id":1543097,"title":"","content":"I do think playing someone who isn't cursed kind of goes against the theme of Curseborne where you specifically play as one of the accursed. I'm also pretty sure it'll happen at some point, Hunter type games are popular.<br /> <br /> Hell, my Bathorite character I've made is a former Hunter before becoming accursed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T12:04:27-07:00","id":1543115,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess it depends on what we mean by hunter. Is it just a human doing the same sorts of things that Curseborne characters do? That seems fine to me and doesn\u2019t even require any special rules or supplements. What ever reasons bind together the other characters could apply to a human.<br /> <br /> Are hunters humans who specifically go out to kill Curseborne? If so, then that would obviously be a very different sort of game, where the characters are humans and the adversaries are Curseborne. Once again, I don\u2019t think that would require special rules, though a supplement for that with flavor text, chronicle ideas, hunter organizations would be cool - like the old Hunters Hunted book for V:tM. <br /> <br /> What about \u201chuman\u201d hunters with magical abilities? I don\u2019t know, I suppose my personal opinion is that giving hunters supernatural abilities undermines the point of being humans fighting against supernaturals. In this context, that could be another Curseborne lineage whose supernatural nature and powers are a little more subtle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T13:43:26-07:00","id":1543120,"title":"","content":"The lack of playing a normal human in the core colors my expectations, but at this point, I also want to see the rest of the corebook before I start getting predictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T18:40:57-07:00","id":1543130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543115#post1543115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I guess it depends on what we mean by hunter. Is it just a human doing the same sorts of things that Curseborne characters do? That seems fine to me and doesn\u2019t even require any special rules or supplements. What ever reasons bind together the other characters could apply to a human.<br /> <br /> Are hunters humans who specifically go out to kill Curseborne? If so, then that would obviously be a very different sort of game, where the characters are humans and the adversaries are Curseborne. Once again, I don\u2019t think that would require special rules, though a supplement for that with flavor text, chronicle ideas, hunter organizations would be cool - like the old Hunters Hunted book for V:tM.<br /> <br /> What about \u201chuman\u201d hunters with magical abilities? I don\u2019t know, I suppose my personal opinion is that giving hunters supernatural abilities undermines the point of being humans fighting against supernaturals. In this context, that could be another Curseborne lineage whose supernatural nature and powers are a little more subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't have enough rules to build a mortal character in the book, so ya, a mortal character, hunter or not, means a different book. And there's a lot of different mortal / hunter books across Chronicles and World that says those roles do appeal to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T19:51:42-07:00","id":1543133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543130#post1543130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't have enough rules to build a mortal character in the book, so ya, a mortal character, hunter or not, means a different book. And there's a lot of different mortal / hunter books across Chronicles and World that says those roles do appeal to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand why one would need a new book to play a human character. It\u2019s just a character that doesn\u2019t have any of the Accursed supernatural powers. A human book could be cool, with information about running a human, human organizations, maybe the occasional special power - but hardly necessary. Just like you could play a human in V:tM before Hunters Hunter came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T21:00:24-07:00","id":1543135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543133#post1543133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t understand why one would need a new book to play a human character. It\u2019s just a character that doesn\u2019t have any of the Accursed supernatural powers. A human book could be cool, with information about running a human, human organizations, maybe the occasional special power - but hardly necessary. Just like you could play a human in V:tM before Hunters Hunter came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your attributes come from your minor and major path, tell me what's a mortal's minor and major path? What's their attribute spread? How many attribute dots total do they get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T21:22:52-07:00","id":1543136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543133#post1543133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t understand why one would need a new book to play a human character. <u>It\u2019s just a character that doesn\u2019t have any of the Accursed supernatural powers</u>. A human book could be cool, with information about running a human, human organizations, maybe the occasional special power - but hardly necessary. <u>Just like you could play a human in V:tM before Hunters Hunter came out.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>From my experience, these two lines feel....limited, in terms of scope. Let me see if I can explain why.<br /> <br /> On that first one, I suppose the biggest problem is that we don't have a solid sense of what the lines for cutting the difference are at this point in two ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Our understanding of textual* standards for character skills is limited to a demo and a chapter we don't have, so we don't have a sense on if the book presents averages <i>based</i> on being human against being an <i>Accursed</i> character as it lands for the game moving forward. If we're told 6 is an average dice pool** for humans, it's easier to run humans without the clutter of the Accursed from that, but if it's just presented as the averages without context, then we need to make guesses that can lead to the math being weird.<br /> 2) We don't know how many of the traits are intended to be built on the fact that you're an Accursed without accounting for the prior humanity. Going with a case example from Chronicles again, if you tried to build a human from any of the gamelines from Chapter 3*** alone, then you'd run into the problems with how their Anchors or Integrity-alikes are really supposed to work with humans, for instance, whether it's trying to reverse engineer Cover, Clarity, or Harmony back into something <i>relevant</i> to both playing humans in general or in specific to each gameline.<br /> <br /> And none of that is even accounting for if the game design is even built to really facilitate that smoothly enough, which....<br /> <br /> Well, this brings me to the second part, because you would have a very bad time playing a human in V:tM before Hunter Hunted****, precisely because Masquerade was built on the assumption that what players needed to know was centered on the vampiric condition unrelated to the human condition, and in fact only assumes Hunters are a problem for vampires within their early character growth/arcs.<br /> <br /> It's not that there's nothing to work with, but a lot of Masquerade's early mechanics either build on being a vampire in a such a way you would obviously remove it, or are built out of such things. Even in the 20th Anniversary edition, something like Willpower, that has a lot of mechanical usage, is still rooted in the vampiric Virtue of Courage, which is built around, well, the concerns of a vampire-and while it's easy to just switch that around to the sort of character resilience you'd want to see in a mortal character, you still have to do that work, nevermind figuring out how much higher or lower it's supposed to be in contrast to make a entertainingly challenging experience. Some mechanics get even harsher cut offs and present no easy opportunities.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why Hunters Hunted included that information, and why that was a particular point of praise for Chronicles when it was released back in 2004 even when it was dealing with all of it's other controversies.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, this is why I'm waiting on the rest of the text. It may be doable with homebrewing, but I'd rather know for sure how much, if any, homebrewing I'm looking at.<br /> -<br /> As for the post on the whole, while I would like it on record I'm <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1312809-does-hunter-need-to-be-an-independent-line?p=1312814#post1312814\">against making Vigil's mistakes again</a>, a book of tools for playing humans who deal with Curseborne's supernaturals as well as going into what that <i>means</i> in Curseborne's context is never a bad idea, particularly since not everyone comes in prepared to problem solve for that particular kind of issue. Investigating and hunting monsters in Curseborne is going to also means the idea needs to work within the themes and metaphysics <i>of</i> Curseborne, and getting into the headspace for that can definitely be worth a book on it's own.<br /> <br /> Plus Hunters Hunted and Vigil shows here's money for doing it, so.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I don't want to dismiss videos and text provided elsewhere for anyone else, but since we're at a point where the penny of execution is about to land on a side with getting backer manuscripts, I'm not at a point where I would want to rely on them, instead wanting to confirm with the actual text from the product as it is right now.<br /> **probably not, but running on old numbers.<br /> ***Chapter 4 provides elaboration for humans on things, but given some things get cut, there have been a few books that does not give you enough to run them as a player character out of the book. I'll have to dig up the particular exceptions I'm referring to later on for ya.<br /> ****Arguably, you <i>still</i> have a bad time playing humans after Hunters Hunted, but that's outside of the purview of this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-05-2024, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T16:50:45-07:00","id":1543170,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a Mortal Hunter just be a Storypath Ultra core character without any template on it? Maybe give it Origin, Role, and Society Paths in line with Hunting, but I don't see how you would make a template for a normal person, unless you were going for a more Mortal+ type character.<br /> <br /> Given that Venators are a key antagonist type in the setting and the variety of them, maybe I could see having a Curseborne: Venator book somewhere down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T21:59:06-07:00","id":1543184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543170#post1543170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a Mortal Hunter just be a Storypath Ultra core character without any template on it? Maybe give it Origin, Role, and Society Paths in line with Hunting, but I don't see how you would make a template for a normal person, unless you were going for a more Mortal+ type character.<br /> <br /> Given that Venators are a key antagonist type in the setting and the variety of them, maybe I could see having a Curseborne: Venator book somewhere down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno! We still haven't seen character creation as it is in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> (again, apologies for people who have watched the videos and are thus understandably frustrated with me, but again, I want to confirm what's in text rather than working secondhand)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T12:52:07-07:00","id":1543208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-\u2013-mortal-hunters?p=1543170#post1543170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a Mortal Hunter just be a Storypath Ultra core character without any template on it? Maybe give it Origin, Role, and Society Paths in line with Hunting, but I don't see how you would make a template for a normal person, unless you were going for a more Mortal+ type character.<br /> <br /> Given that Venators are a key antagonist type in the setting and the variety of them, maybe I could see having a Curseborne: Venator book somewhere down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a different book. But it's been said the different storypath games aren't meant to be used together, so while I imagine it would be similar it likely wouldn't be exactly the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:49:12-07:00","id":1543216,"title":"","content":"You could just choose any minor and major path that you like. <i>Voila</i>. I guess that\u2019s technically home-brew, but just barely. I\u2019m not against a hunter sourcebook, I think it\u2019s a cool idea. I\u2019m just saying that it isn\u2019t strictly needed.<br /> <br /> On a slightly related topic, I wonder if there will be any kind of mechanism for true faith or something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:52:31-07:00","id":1543217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"h